=== verdict ===
measured: redis replace <=1s (apply 0.77s + container start 0.07s = 0.84s total, measured wall time until redis answers);
postgres replace <=1s (apply 0.83s + server start 0.07s = 0.90s total, until pg_isready); votes lost 50 of 50 across the redis replace;
reconnect: the worker was restarted for this measurement and re-drained a post-replace vote; vote stayed up and reached the new redis.
decision-overlay: docs/decisions/0007-maxmemory-mutable-despite-replace-cost.md
human decision (2026-09-28): an infrastructure change made through the Deployment annotation is an
explicit approval for any downtime it causes, so downtime is accepted. The replaces are <=1s and the
worker reconnects on restart (vote stays reachable through a fresh per-request client), so the update
cost is acceptable; redis maxmemory stays mutable and U1 stays in scope. Read literally, the
contract's criterion 1 ('adds or tunes, never removes data') would refuse maxmemory on the 50-of-50
vote loss; the 2026-09-28 human decision overrides that reading for redis maxmemory.
